{"content":[{"c":["MAGOR-MISSABIB*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Name given by Jeremiah to Pashhur, the chief officer in the house of the Lord. Jeremiah did this because Pashhur put him in stocks for prophesying judgment upon Judah (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.19.14-20.2","r":"Jer.19.14-20.2","rawR":"Jer.19.14-20.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.19.14-20.2","value":"Jer.19.14-20.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 19:14–20:2"},"). The name Pashhur means “prosperity round about” and was changed to “terror on every side” (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.20.3","r":"Jer.20.3","rawR":"Jer.20.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.20.3","value":"Jer.20.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"20:3"},") because Pashhur was to see the horrors of the Babylonian invasion."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"MagorMissabib","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jer 19:14–20:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.19.14-20.2","rawQueryValue":"Jer.19.14-20.2","sourceRefExact":"Jer.19.14-20.2"},{"anchorText":"20:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.20.3","rawQueryValue":"Jer.20.3","sourceRefExact":"Jer.20.3"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ebdc857103cf5f070a8027af5e7426ddfe161fac38967e5722dd1ca328ba4ed5","sourceItemName":"MagorMissabib","sourceItemOrder":51,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"MagorMissabib","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Magor-Missabib*","title":"Magor-Missabib*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}